# The build context is the workspace root, because armory-server depends on
# armory-core by path and a context of `server/` alone cannot see it. That
# makes this file matter before the first build rather than after: `target/`
# alone is gigabytes, and it is uploaded to the daemon before any instruction
# in the Containerfile runs.
#
# The Containerfile then copies an explicit list rather than the whole context,
# so this only has to stop the large and the secret.
target/
.git/
.flatpak-build/
dist/

# The GTK half. armory-server compiles none of it, and `data/` is eight
# megabytes of zone and instance JSON that only the shell links in.
src/
tests/
examples/
packaging/
addon/
docs/
scripts/

# These reach the container through the environment, never through a layer,
# where they would survive in the image whatever the running process does.
server/.env
packaging/.env
